One morning, Sound discovered she could shape the cave walls with her voice. High notes carved smooth arches, low notes formed deep chambers. She sang for centuries, sculpting an enormous labyrinth of tunnels and grottos.

As her final masterpiece, Sound sang her most powerful note yet—a pure, sustained tone that shook the entire cave. The walls trembled and began singing back to her. For the first time, Sound heard herself. The cave returned her voice, transformed but recognizable.

Overwhelmed with joy, Sound sang louder, and the cave answered louder still. She whispered, and gentle echoes whispered back. She had created the first conversation.

